      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T17:25:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think these cases are effectively missing from `it83xx_tcpm_switch_plug_out_type`, which treats CC open the same as Rp detected and I think does nothing in the powered-cable-only case. Would it be sufficient to add these cases to that function?\n\nAs far as the LPM debounce window goes, I think the TCPM should be actively checking in `check_drp_connection` before entering LPM. Is there a race window right as this detection setting changes?",
      "revId": "384d133828ae7886b7e51d0000d8b0b715e9c34c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
